+    "field": "practice_questions",
+    "path": "[5].marks",
+    "expect": "Students may include:\n• Jazz elements across all three: extended and added-note chords, ii–V–I progressions with sevenths, blue notes, improvised solo sections, scat singing, fretless bass and double bass.\n• Brazilian samba elements: ganza, caixa, congas and triangle; off-beat piano chords creating a double-time samba feel; layered syncopation becoming polyrhythm — though with unusual features (3/4 passages, no son clave).\n• Chamber/classical elements in Little Fly: a through-scored string trio, arco/tremolo/double-stopping techniques, a Blake poem set syllabically in E major.\n• Top-band answers frame each observation as a named tradition meeting another, with located examples.",
+    "value": "Students may include:\n• Jazz elements across all three: extended and added-note chords, ii–V–I progressions with sevenths, blue notes, improvised solo sections, scat singing, fretless bass and double bass.\n• Brazilian samba elements: ganza, caixa, congas and triangle; off-beat piano chords creating a double-time samba feel; layered syncopation becoming polyrhythm — though with unusual features (3/4 passages, no son clave).\n• Chamber/classical elements in Little Fly: a through-scored string trio, arco/tremolo/double-stopping techniques, a Blake poem set syllabically in E major.\n• Strong answers connect named traditions to located examples.",
